.TH SAPHIRA-CLUSTER 8 "October 2026" "saphira-cluster 0.1.0" "Saphira"
.SH NAME
saphira-cluster \- configure and protect Saphira hosts for Slurm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-cluster
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-cluster
is the Saphira cluster control utility.
It discovers local capability, applies the Saphira service-reservation
policy, generates and validates Slurm configuration, manages node
enrolment, and reports cluster state.
.PP
It is not a scheduler.
Slurm schedules compute; LVS/ldirectord distribute service traffic;
.B saphira-cluster
configures and protects the hosts.
.PP
This is reserved-capacity clustering: Slurm is told only the resources
left after statically reserving service capacity, and it schedules
exactly that.
Dynamic idle harvesting is explicitly out of scope for v1.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
.IB name " --controller " host
Start a new cluster definition. Unimplemented in the scaffold.
.TP
.BI "node add " host " [--reserve-cpus " N "] [--reserve-memory " SIZE "] [--gpu " auto "] [--gpu-share " SPEC "] [--no-exec]"
Enrol a node. Unimplemented in the scaffold.
.TP
.BI "node remove " host
Drop a node. Unimplemented in the scaffold.
.TP
.B apply
Write generated configuration. Unimplemented in the scaffold.
.TP
.B validate
Check generated configuration. Unimplemented in the scaffold.
.TP
.B status
Show cluster state. Unimplemented in the scaffold.
.TP
.B resources
Show local CPU, memory and GPU capability, read-only.
.TP
.B doctor
Run read-only node health checks: hostname resolution, IPv6, clock
synchronisation, cgroup v2, the slurm identity, Slurm version-line
consistency, Slurm ports, and
.BR slurmd " -C"
capability output. Changes nothing. Never alters firewall rules.
.TP
.B help
Show help text.
.TP
.B version
Show version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show help text; accepted anywhere.
.TP
.B --version
Show version; accepted anywhere.
.SH "EXIT CODES"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error.
.TP
.B 2
A
.B doctor
check failed.
.TP
.B 3
Parsed, but not implemented in this scaffold.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/slurm/slurm.conf
Live controller configuration, generated on the target.
Never shipped in a package, never committed.
.TP
.I /etc/slurm/slurmdbd.conf
Live accounting configuration, generated on the target.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sinfo (1),
.BR srun (1),
.BR slurm.conf (5)
.SH NOTES
Package payloads, service units and tests in this project are
site-neutral and use generic placeholders
.RI ( controller ,
.IR node01 ,
.IR node02 ).
Real-machine walkthroughs live in the project documentation only.
